    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42954" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσσήν</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆνος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>priest of Artemis</i> of Ephesus, in pl., <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				352.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				363.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.13.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>king,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Jov.</u>
					66
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυρμιδόνων ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Aet.</u>
					1.1.23
				</span></i>
			 (expld. as,=<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκιστής</span> by
				Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.923
			</span></i>) : prop. <i>king bee</i> (i. e. <i>queen bee</i>), acc.
			to <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				383.31
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑσσήν</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				1.1.23
			</span></i> (Pap.), perh. because of supposed connexion with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑσμός, ἕσσαι,</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσσάω.</span>)</div>
